Feature: Patient Account Table Creation and Data Transformation

  The system must create the target table purgo_playground.patient_account in Unity Catalog purgo_databricks, 
  by transforming and loading data from purgo_playground.pa_account according to the mapping specification.
  The process must enforce all schema, transformation, validation, and error handling rules as described.

  Background:
    Given the source table purgo_playground.pa_account exists in Unity Catalog purgo_databricks
    And the mapping specification from source_target_mapping_specification (1).xlsx is available
    And the target table purgo_playground.patient_account must be created with the following schema:
      | Column Name                  | Datatype  | Nullable | Logic/Source                                                                 |
      |-----------------------------|-----------|----------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
      | patient_foundation_shipment | string    | NOT NULL | pa_account.patient_foundation_shipment (straight move)                       |
      | prescriber_id               | string    | NOT NULL | If "Dr." not in prefix, prepend "DR." to pa_account.prescriber_name_c        |
      | prescriber_key              | string    | NOT NULL | If "Dr." not in prefix, prepend "DR." to pa_account.prescriber_name_c_address|
      | patient_sf_id               | string    | NOT NULL | pa_account.patinet_c (straight move)                                         |
      | service_request_type        | string    | NOT NULL | pa_account.recordtypeid (straight move)                                      |
      | case_sf_id                  | string    | NOT NULL | pa_account.id (straight move)                                                |
      | account_id                  | string    | NOT NULL | pa_account.accountid (straight move)                                         |
      | hash_key                    | string    | NOT NULL | Concatenate patinet_c#recordtypeid#id#accountid                              |
      | last_modified_date          | timestamp | NOT NULL | Current timestamp (ETL run time)                                             |
      | planned_date                | date      | NULLABLE | No mapping provided, set to NULL                                             |
    And if purgo_playground.patient_account already exists, it must be dropped before creation
    And only records from Salesforce source system must be considered
    And only mapped columns must be included in the target table
    And all NOT NULL columns must be populated; if source value is NULL, record must be skipped and error logged
    And records must be filtered to only include those where patinet_c contains substring "PAT" (case-insensitive)
    And if duplicate hash_key values are generated, the record must be skipped and error logged
    And Unity Catalog/Databricks SQL syntax must be used for table creation

  Scenario: Drop and Create Target Table
    Given the target table purgo_playground.patient_account may already exist
    When the ETL process starts
    Then the table purgo_playground.patient_account must be dropped if it exists
    And the table must be created with the schema as specified in the Background

  Scenario Outline: Transform and Load Valid Patient Account Records
    Given a source record in purgo_playground.pa_account with the following values:
      | patient_foundation_shipment | prescriber_name_c | prescriber_name_c_address | patinet_c | recordtypeid | id | accountid |
      | <patient_foundation_shipment> | <prescriber_name_c> | <prescriber_name_c_address> | <patinet_c> | <recordtypeid> | <id> | <accountid> |
    And patinet_c contains substring "PAT" (case-insensitive)
    And all source columns required for NOT NULL target columns are NOT NULL
    And the hash_key value <hash_key> is unique in the target table
    When the ETL process transforms and loads the record
    Then the following target record must be created in purgo_playground.patient_account:
      | patient_foundation_shipment | prescriber_id | prescriber_key | patient_sf_id | service_request_type | case_sf_id | account_id | hash_key | last_modified_date | planned_date |
      | <patient_foundation_shipment> | <prescriber_id> | <prescriber_key> | <patinet_c> | <recordtypeid> | <id> | <accountid> | <hash_key> | <current_timestamp> | NULL |
    And prescriber_id is "<prescriber_id>" where:
      - If <prescriber_name_c> starts with "Dr." (case-insensitive), use as is
      - Else, prepend "DR." to <prescriber_name_c>
    And prescriber_key is "<prescriber_key>" where:
      - If <prescriber_name_c_address> starts with "Dr." (case-insensitive), use as is
      - Else, prepend "DR." to <prescriber_name_c_address>
    And hash_key is the concatenation of <patinet_c>#<recordtypeid>#<id>#<accountid>
    And last_modified_date is set to the ETL run current timestamp
    And planned_date is set to NULL

    Examples:
      | patient_foundation_shipment | prescriber_name_c | prescriber_name_c_address | patinet_c   | recordtypeid | id         | accountid   | prescriber_id         | prescriber_key           | hash_key                                 |
      | "SHIP123"                  | "Dr. John Smith"  | "Dr. Jane Doe"           | "PAT001"    | "SRV"        | "CASE001"  | "ACC001"    | "Dr. John Smith"      | "Dr. Jane Doe"           | "PAT001#SRV#CASE001#ACC001"              |
      | "SHIP456"                  | "John Smith"      | "Jane Doe"               | "pat002"    | "SRV2"       | "CASE002"  | "ACC002"    | "DR. John Smith"      | "DR. Jane Doe"           | "pat002#SRV2#CASE002#ACC002"             |
      | "SHIP789"                  | "DR. Alice"       | "DR. Bob"                | "Pat003"    | "SRV3"       | "CASE003"  | "ACC003"    | "DR. Alice"           | "DR. Bob"                | "Pat003#SRV3#CASE003#ACC003"             |

  Scenario Outline: Skip Record if patinet_c Does Not Contain "PAT"
    Given a source record in purgo_playground.pa_account with patinet_c value <patinet_c>
    When the ETL process checks the filter condition
    Then the record must be skipped
    And an error must be logged with:
      | error_col | error_message | event_time | hash_key |
      | "patinet_c" | "patinet_c does not contain 'PAT'" | <current_timestamp> | <hash_key> |

    Examples:
      | patinet_c | hash_key                |
      | "123456"  | "123456#SRV#CASE001#ACC001" |
      | "ABCDEF"  | "ABCDEF#SRV2#CASE002#ACC002" |

  Scenario Outline: Skip Record if Source Value for NOT NULL Column is NULL
    Given a source record in purgo_playground.pa_account with a NULL value in <null_col>
    And patinet_c contains substring "PAT" (case-insensitive)
    When the ETL process checks for NOT NULL enforcement
    Then the record must be skipped
    And an error must be logged with:
      | error_col | error_message | event_time | hash_key |
      | <null_col> | "<null_col> is NULL for NOT NULL target column" | <current_timestamp> | <hash_key> |

    Examples:
      | null_col                  | hash_key                                 |
      | "patient_foundation_shipment" | "PAT001#SRV#CASE001#ACC001"              |
      | "prescriber_name_c"           | "PAT002#SRV2#CASE002#ACC002"             |
      | "recordtypeid"                | "PAT003#SRV3#CASE003#ACC003"             |
      | "id"                          | "PAT004#SRV4#CASE004#ACC004"             |
      | "accountid"                   | "PAT005#SRV5#CASE005#ACC005"             |

  Scenario Outline: Skip Record if Duplicate hash_key is Generated
    Given a source record in purgo_playground.pa_account with hash_key value <hash_key>
    And a record with hash_key <hash_key> already exists in purgo_playground.patient_account
    When the ETL process checks for hash_key uniqueness
    Then the record must be skipped
    And an error must be logged with:
      | error_col | error_message | event_time | hash_key |
      | "hash_key" | "Duplicate hash_key value" | <current_timestamp> | <hash_key> |

    Examples:
      | hash_key                                 |
      | "PAT001#SRV#CASE001#ACC001"              |
      | "pat002#SRV2#CASE002#ACC002"             |

  Scenario Outline: Error Handling for Data Type Mismatch
    Given a source record in purgo_playground.pa_account with value <invalid_value> in <col>
    And the value does not conform to the expected datatype for the target column
    When the ETL process attempts to transform and load the record
    Then the record must be skipped
    And an error must be logged with:
      | error_col | error_message | event_time | hash_key |
      | <col> | "Data type mismatch for <col>: <invalid_value>" | <current_timestamp> | <hash_key> |

    Examples:
      | col                        | invalid_value | hash_key                                 |
      | "patient_foundation_shipment" | 12345         | "PAT001#SRV#CASE001#ACC001"              |
      | "recordtypeid"                | NULL          | "PAT002#SRV2#CASE002#ACC002"             |

  Scenario: Only Mapped Columns Are Included in Target Table
    Given the mapping specification lists only specific columns for patient_account
    When the ETL process creates the target table
    Then only the mapped columns must be present in purgo_playground.patient_account
    And any additional columns from the source table must be ignored

  Scenario: Planned Date Column is Always NULL
    Given the planned_date column in purgo_playground.patient_account has no mapping or source value
    When the ETL process loads records
    Then planned_date must be set to NULL for all records

  Scenario: Use Unity Catalog/Databricks SQL Syntax for Table Creation
    Given the ETL process is running in Unity Catalog purgo_databricks
    When the table purgo_playground.patient_account is created
    Then Databricks SQL/Unity Catalog syntax must be used for DROP TABLE IF EXISTS and CREATE TABLE statements

  Scenario: Only Salesforce Source System Records Are Processed
    Given the source table purgo_playground.pa_account may contain records from multiple source systems
    When the ETL process loads data
    Then only records where source system is "Salesforce" must be processed

  Scenario: Error Logging for Skipped Records
    Given a record is skipped due to filter, NULL, duplicate hash_key, or data type mismatch
    When the ETL process logs the error
    Then the error must be recorded in purgo_playground.pat_account_error_log with:
      | hash_key | error_col | error_message | event_time |
    And event_time must be set to the ETL run current timestamp

